## 6. Gaps recovered from related data

| Gap | Recovered from |
|---|---|
| Missing start or end time of a flow event | The next or previous step in the same visit (registration ends when triage starts, and so on) |
| Missing bed discharge time | The Discharge event start of the same encounter |
| Invalid department on a bed | The ward name (each ward belongs to one department) |
| Missing department capacity | The number of beds in that department |
| Wrong shift type or scheduled times | The scheduled start time and the shift date |
| Missing actual start or end of a shift | The other actual time and the actual hours |
| Missing holiday name | The same date in the other year (fixed-date holidays only) |
| Missing department on a staffing requirement | Elimination: each date, shift and acuity level must contain all eight departments exactly once |
| Missing calendar dates | Rebuilding the full 2025–2026 date range |

## 7. Business rules applied

- Waiting time can never be longer than the step it belongs to.
- A bed is operational only when its status is Available; ER and ICU wards hold only Emergency and ICU beds.
- An employee works at most one shift a day, and only active employees work shifts.
- A patient's bed must belong to the patient's department; when one stay appears with two beds, the matching bed is kept.
- Experience cannot be less than the years since joining.
- Transferred patients always have disposition Transfer; a patient with a discharge time is not "Admitted".

## 8. Validation

1. **Against the original data:** 99.96% of filled-in cells match the error-free source. Remaining differences come from judgement calls on conflicting duplicates and from shift end times that are a few minutes out.
2. **Against the database:** the tables load with primary keys, foreign keys and CHECK rules, and `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` returns 0 problems.
3. **Rule checks:** no reversed times, no negative stays, no duplicate keys, no overlapping bed stays.

